# Curated flow-type-resolver behavioral eval fixture. One {id,prompt,expected} per line;
# `#`/`//` lines are skipped by the scorer. `expected` is a canonical
# taxonomy specCategory.
#
# COVERAGE NOTE (project-codey port): this 60-prompt fixture covers the 10 families the
# source PR shipped plus IndivRelatedRecord (Engagement / Journey-Triggered, family
# FT-IRR), added for the individual-related-record routing and $Input record-context
# work. It still has NO prompts for the other four trigger categories added during the
# project-codey port (AutomationEvent, List, CampaignMember, RecordQuery). Running this
# fixture validates the covered families did not REGRESS; it does NOT validate those
# four categories. See CURATION.md.
#
# STATUS: OVERALL accuracy gated at 0.95. Source PR scored 98.2% (56/57 on the original
# families); the lone miss is FT-AUTO-003 (button-invoked flat Autolaunched flow read as
# Screen), kept as an honest hard case rather than dropped. This fixture adds the FT-IRR
# family for 60 prompts total, then the FT-FORM family (FormSubmissionEvent, plus a
# Screen look-alike and an Automation Event-worded prompt that must still resolve to
# FormSubmissionEvent) for 63, then the FT-CRM family for 70. FT-CRM rows carry
# "expectAsk": a CRM Triggered Flow ("CRM Triggered" / "CRM Trigger") request that says
# "marketing" resolves to IndivRelatedRecord with no question; one that does not say
# "marketing" leans IndivRelatedRecord but must ask (marketing Automation Event or
# Record-Triggered Flow). Two look-alikes must not route there at all (a plain Contact
# update with no CRM Triggered name stays RecordTriggered; a Data Cloud DMO change stays
# DataCloudDataChange). The FT-OND family (OnDemandNoTrigger) brings it to 77: an On-Demand
# Flow request and an "autolaunched" marketing send that the API starts for one person
# resolve to OnDemand; an "on-demand flow" that Apex calls with no marketing send, and an
# autolaunched flow that sends a plain email, stay Autolaunched; an On-Demand Flow named as
# the type stays OnDemand even with no send. An API-started email "with consent from" a
# subscription is a marketing send (OnDemand) even though the prompt never says marketing;
# an API-started Email Alert stays Autolaunched. FT-IRR-004..006 bring it to 80: a user's
# request word for word, a marketing "automation event flow" that triggers when a Lead's
# status is Nurturing and sends to a journey, resolves to IndivRelatedRecord with no
# question; the same Lead change with no marketing action stays RecordTriggered; and a
# marketing "automation event flow" that starts on an email link click stays AutomationEvent.
# FT-OND and FT-IRR-004..006 predictions were produced blind by an agent that read only
# flow-type-resolver.md and taxonomy.json.
